title: Payers › Workflow Builder › Configure a step › Integrations
route: /payers/summit?tab=builder
intro: Integration steps (EMR sync, payer portal, API request, webhook, fax, email, external task system, custom integration) show a connection status and never take a secret. Credentials are managed outside the app. Connected is shown only for what EMR Connect really has connected; everything else says Demo simulation or Not configured.
dir: TD
---
start s1 "Select an integration step"
screen cn "A box 'Connection: ...'\nthen 'Credentials are managed outside this app. Nothing secret is entered or stored here.'"
decision d1 "Which status?"
screen k1 "Connected\nOnly EMR sync, and only when EMR Connect has a system connected\n'Clinical record · Site A ... connected in EMR Connect. The sync itself is a demo simulation.'"
screen k2 "Demo simulation\nPayer portal and Fax: the demo pretends the connection works, nothing leaves the app"
screen k3 "Not configured\nAPI request, Webhook, Email, External task system, Custom integration,\nand EMR sync when no record system is connected"
screen fl "Fields\n'Action' (for example check the status, submit, upload)\n'If it is not connected' (A person does it by hand, or No fallback: stop and ask)\n'What to send' under Advanced (the data it carries, never a secret)"
process p1 "Steps that reach the payer carry 'A person approves first', always on"
process p2 "When a step is not connected, a test run says so\nand follows the fallback chosen"
decision d2 "Is anything typed that looks like a password or a key?"
process p3 "There is no field for one: the app has nowhere to keep it"
click c1 "Open EMR Connect to see what is connected"
goto g1 "Continues in: EMR Connect › Connected systems › What each status means"
goto g2 "Continues in: Payers › Test Workflow › Run a test case"
end e1 "The step says exactly how real it is"

s1 --> cn --> d1
d1 -->|Connected| k1 --> fl
d1 -->|Demo| k2 --> fl
d1 -->|Not set up| k3 --> fl
fl --> p1 --> p2 --> e1
cn --> d2
d2 -->|Yes| p3 --> e1
d2 -->|No| fl
k1 --> c1 --> g1
p2 --> g2
